    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im working on a new screenplay and i want to make sure i'm not accidentally leaning too hard into cliches. i have a few character bios drafted and i need a professional eye. can u look at these and tell me if any of them feel like 'tropes'? also, based on their vibes, which ones do u think would fit better in a gritty crime drama vs a high-society prestige drama?\n\nhere are the bios:\n\n1. Marcus: Mid-30s, very observant, always has a bit of a defensive edge to his posture, knows how to navigate the streets of the city.\n2. Elena: Late 40s, impeccably dressed, highly influential in her social circle, speaks with a very controlled and polished manner.\n3. Kenji: 20s, extremely focused, highly technical, tends to be more of a quiet observer in group settings.\n4. Julian: Early 50s, charismatic, comes from old money, handles high-stakes negotiations with ease.\n5. Andre: Late 20s, quick-witted, has a lot of energy, often found in loud or crowded environments.\n\nthoughts?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
